# ---- pause-flag row cache (optional, BH-5004) ----
# flag_active (bin/lib/jobs/flags.sh) decides from the pause_flags row, and
# remembers each row it read for this many seconds inside one process, so a
# lane that checks the same flag in a per-PR loop makes one GET per name per
# TTL instead of one per call. An outage is remembered the same way: one failed
# request per name per TTL. 0 turns the cache off (a GET on every call). A
# value that is not a whole number means the default. A console pause or resume
# reaches a process that already read the flag up to this much later.
#FLAG_ROW_TTL_S=10
